/*!
    \page data-handling.html
    \title Data Handling
    \brief Supply records to DashboardView using supported data formats.

    Dashboard data is represented as a list of objects. Each object describes
    one record, and its keys become field names available to dashboard widgets.

    \section1 Set Data Directly

    Use \c setData() with a JavaScript array of objects:

    \qml
    DashboardView {
        id: dashboard

        Component.onCompleted: {
            dashboard.setData([
                { category: "Online", sales: 240, orders: 120 },
                { category: "Retail", sales: 185, orders: 94 }
            ])
        }
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 JSON

    \c loadJson() accepts a JSON array of objects or a JSON object containing
    a \c data or \c rows array. Each row must be a JSON object.

    \section1 CSV

    \c loadCsv() accepts CSV text with a header row. The following rows are
    interpreted as records. Quoted CSV fields are supported by the data source.

    \section1 Local Files

    \c loadFile() loads a local JSON or CSV file using a URL.

    \section1 REST Endpoints

    \c loadRest() retrieves JSON from an HTTP or HTTPS endpoint. The optional
    second argument is a Bearer token. The response must have the same accepted
    JSON structure as \c loadJson().

    \section1 C++ Models

    Set the \c dataModel property to a Qt item model, or call
    \c setDataModel() with a model object. The model's role names are used as
    dashboard field names.

    \section1 Errors and Loading State

    \c loading indicates whether a remote request is in progress.
    \c dataLoadFailed(message) is emitted when the data source reports an
    error. The underlying \l DashboardDataSource also exposes \c errorMessage.
*/
